+ * and the cooldown seconds between them (flat candles included). The server batch REPLACES the
+ * store on connect/resync; candleClosed appends one bar per second; priceUpdate only moves the
+ * in-progress bar. This component therefore:
+ *   - `setData` only when the store's batch generation changes (replace) or when the tab becomes
+ *     visible again; `update` for everything else. Nothing is torn down at round boundaries — only
+ *     the ROUND ENTRY line moves.
+ *   - keeps the viewport FIXED: barSpacing = plotWidth / 80, rightOffset = 18, applied on create
+ *     and on resize. Never `setVisibleRange` over N bars, never a re-zoom at a round boundary.
+ *   - draws the time cursor at the server's "now": x = pixel(newest bar) + fraction × live bar
+ *     spacing, with the fraction measured on the server clock (see chartClockService). Because
+ *     the stream keeps producing a bar per second through the cooldown, the cursor stays where
+ *     the round ended and glides right, exactly like the bars around it.
